<Base title="Workshop Sessions — Groove Dice expansion | Kim’s Work" description={p.summary}>
<article class="wrap guide"><a class="back" href={url('software/expansions/')}>← Expansions</a><p class="eyebrow">FOR GROOVE DICE / VERSION {p.version}</p><h1>Workshop Sessions.</h1><p class="lead">{p.summary}</p><a class="button" href={p.asset}>Download .gdexp ↓</a><p><a href={p.release}>Release notes & checksum ↗</a> · Requires <a href={url('plugins/groove-dice/')}>Groove Dice 1.0.0</a>.</p><section><h2>Original sounds. A separate payload.</h2><p>Kick, snare, closed/open hats, clap, tom, cymbal and percussion are procedurally synthesized for this project. No third-party sample recordings or MIDI are included. Eight kits are configurations of the 32 included one-shots.</p><p>This pack was exported from the actual Pack Builder desktop UI. The source sounds are drawn from the original core, so it demonstrates custom combinations and the expansion workflow rather than claiming 32 sounds exclusive to this pack.</p></section><section><h2>Install</h2><ol><li>Download and unzip <a href={url('apps/groove-dice-pack-builder/')}>Pack Builder</a>.</li><li>Use Manage Packs and choose Content inside your installed kim - VST - Groove Dice folder on a locally accessible MPC drive.</li><li>Install this .gdexp, then reopen Groove Dice. Select Workshop Sessions in the pack filter or choose its kits in the MPC PRESET menu.</li></ol><p>Core and other installed packs stay separate. Removing a required pack can leave missing sounds in saved songs; keep its .gdexp to reinstall it. This format is specific to Groove Dice, not native MPC XPN.</p></section></article></Base>
